 ],
 "notes": "Armory modal, Warband tab selected (tab.warband has the lit gold frame, warm label colour and diamond finials top/bottom; the other four tabs are idle navy). Same modal chrome as spells.json (modal, header, tabs, close). Header subtitle reads 'SQUAD 5 / 6' and is split into a caption (subtitle) and a dynamic count (subtitle.count) because the concept's word gap is wider than Cinzel's. Squad strip: six unit cards, taller than the spell slots (109 px, so the strip panel runs to y 268 and the lower panels start at 272, 8 px lower than in spells). Slots 1-5 hold Lv 1 units, each with 1 of 4 pips filled: 1 swordsman with shield, 2 archer, 3 archer (selected: glowing orange frame, 1 px taller, warm badge), 4 shield bearer, 5 spearman. The spearman's spear tip pokes 4 px above the card top, so slot.5.art starts above the card. Slot 6 is empty (grey plus and 'Empty slot'; no class icon, level or pips). Number badges are gold plates in each card's top-left corner with black serif numerals. The concept numerals are taller and narrower than Crimson (ink 16 px tall), so the width-fitted size draws them shorter (same as spells). Unit collection: 3x3 grid of uniform cells (94x91, columns at 51/154/258, rows at 348/450/552). Each cell has a dark corner tab with a gold class icon and a unit picture. There is no level text and no pips in the cells on this screen. grid.0.1 (Archer) is selected with the orange glow frame, which reaches about 1 px outside the cell rect. All 9 cells are fully visible. The scrollbar is a gold track with end caps (344-651) and a hexagonal thumb at 411-449, a little below the top, not at scroll position 0. The concept label reads 'Unit Collection' with a capital C; the game's sentence-case convention would be 'Unit collection' (spells uses 'Spell collection'). The preview well shows the selected Archer on a pedestal with prev/next chevrons. The detail column has no frame: wood on the left and a parchment map with lantern/helmet on the right, bleeding to the modal edge. It shows a bow icon + 'Archer' and 'LEVEL 1' with 1 of 4 pips. 'LEVEL 1' is split into detail.level ('LEVEL') and detail.level.value ('1') because the concept's word gap is wider. detail.level.value gives an explicit size 19 instead of a width, since width-fitting a single narrow glyph would shrink it. A translucent chip shows a class medallion + 'Support \u00b7 Equipped' (no second chip icon on this screen), then a thin gold rule with a small diamond at its left end that fades out to the right. There is no description line. Five stat tiles (2+2+1, icon left, Cinzel caption + Crimson value): HEALTH 48, DAMAGE 10, COURAGE 24, RANGE 146, RECOVERY 8s. All captions have a 9 px cap height (about Cinzel 13), but the width-fit gives 11-13 because the concept letter widths vary. Values are condensed bold figures (ink 19 px tall), so the width-fitted Crimson sizes (23-26) draw them shorter. Buttons: UNEQUIP (navy, left, label centred) and UPGRADE 59 (gold, primary, dark label + gold coin pile icon). UPGRADE and its cost are separate text elements (button.right.label / button.right.cost) because the concept leaves a wider gap before the number, mirroring spells' SCRIBE 134."
}